authors				Junegunn Choi, Simon Hauser and telescope-fzf-native contributors
status				testing

headline			fzf's fuzzy matching algorithm in C
description
	The scorer of the fzf fuzzy finder, ported to C for Telescope (Neovim): fuzzy, exact, prefix, suffix and whole-text matching of a pattern against a text, with fzf's scores (bonuses at word starts, camelCase and after separators) and the positions of the matched characters, and fzf's extended query syntax ('exact ^prefix suffix$ !not a | b).  One C99 file with a C interface, so libsyllable's GCC 4.1.2 C++ uses it as well as C.  libsyllable's os::FuzzyString is built on it.
licenses			MIT

home				github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope-fzf-native.nvim
locations			https://proxy.golang.org/github.com/nvim-telescope/telescope-fzf-native.nvim/@v/

; The project makes no releases: this is commit b25b749b (2026-05-06) of its
; main branch, as the Go module proxy serves it (an immutable zip, checked
; by sum.golang.org: h1:SbEL4hPWsNYt3kyOxSfq2pxNGQralp1RIn+QJY3pQ/A=).
;
; fzf-native-20260506.patch:
; - fzf_suffix_match() (word$) read before the start of a text shorter than
;   the word ("a.h" for ".cpp$"): a size_t difference checked for < 0
; - trailing_whitespaces() read before the start of an empty or
;   all-whitespace text (^word$, word$): a size_t counted down to >= 0
; - strtok_r in place of strtok in fzf_parse_pattern(): strtok's state is
;   shared by every thread
; - extern "C" in fzf.h, for C++
;
; The CMake build (cmake/Ports.cmake, fzf_native) builds this port with
; patches/Makefile in place of the project's (which builds a shared library
; for Lua's FFI): one static library of PIC objects, linked into
; libsyllable with its symbols kept private.  It is not installed on the
; boot volume.
make-file			Makefile

documentation		README.md LICENSE
